CODE 

class Solution:
    def checkString(self, s):
        if ("ba" in s):
            return False
        else:
            return True
        return True


EXPLANATION

The idea is to make sure that no b appears before an a in the string. 
We check whether the substring "ba" exists anywhere using not in. 
If "ba" is found, it means an a appears after a b, so the condition is false. 
If "ba" is not found, all the as must come before the bs, so the function returns True. 
This works because the string only contains a and b.
